@startuml CloudWarehouse_Physical_Architecture
title Physical Architecture — Runtime, Infra Details, Backup (MVP)

skinparam node {
  BackgroundColor #F0F8FF
  BorderColor #2980b9
  FontSize 11
}
skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor #ECF0F1
  BorderColor #34495e
  FontSize 10
}
skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor #E8F8F5
  BorderColor #1ABC9C
}

node "Client PC (LAN or local)" as Client {
  component "Chrome / Edge" as Browser
  note right of Browser
    OS: Windows 10/11
    Access: http://host:5001
  end note
}

node "App + DB host\n(single-machine demo / 师傅机)" as Workstation {
  component "OS: Windows 10/11\n.NET 9 runtime" as OS
  component "Kestrel\nCloudWarehouse.Backend\nHTTP :5001\n(bind 0.0.0.0 or localhost)" as Kestrel
  database "SQL Server\nDB: CloudWarehouse\nTDS :1433\nrecovery: FULL or SIMPLE" as MSSQL
  component "Windows Firewall\ninbound allow TCP 5001\n(optional LAN demo)" as FW
  component "App logs / console\n+ SSMS for ops checks" as Ops
  OS --> Kestrel
  OS --> MSSQL
  FW ..> Kestrel : protects port
  Ops ..> Kestrel
  Ops ..> MSSQL
}

node "Backup landing zone\n(same host or USB/NAS)" as BackupZone {
  component "Manual *.bak files\n+ schema.sql in git\n+ publish zip (app bits)" as Bak
}

cloud "GitHub Cloud (CI only)" as GH {
  component "Git repository" as Repo
  component "Actions runner\nubuntu-latest\nno prod DB link" as Runner
  component "Artifacts:\ncoverage-report\n(+ vuln scan if enabled)" as Art
}

node "Planned redundancy\n(NOT deployed in MVP)" as Planned #E8E8E8 {
  component "IIS / reverse proxy\n+ TLS terminate" as IIS #D0D0D0
  component "Dedicated SQL host\nor Managed SQL" as SQL2 #D0D0D0
  component "Automated daily backup\n+ optional warm standby" as AutoBak #D0D0D0
}

Browser -[#2980b9,thickness=2]-> Kestrel : HTTP :5001\nREST + static wwwroot
Kestrel -[#27ae60,thickness=2]-> MSSQL : ADO.NET / TCP 1433\nconn: DefaultConnection
MSSQL -[#8E44AD,dashed,thickness=2]-> Bak : scheduled manual backup\n(weekly or before demo)
Bak ..[#7F8C8D]> OS : restore path\n(RTO = reinstall app + restore bak)

actor "Developer / Admin" as Dev
Dev -[#E74C3C,dashed]-> Repo : git push (HTTPS)
Runner -[#34495e,dashed]-> Repo : git clone
Runner -[#34495e,dashed]-> Art : upload
Runner -[hidden]-> MSSQL

Workstation ..[dashed,#95A5A6].. Planned : evolve when\nmulti-user / uptime required

note right of Kestrel
  **Port map**
  - 5001/tcp HTTP (app)
  - 1433/tcp SQL (loopback or LAN)
  **App bits**
  - wwwroot/ static UI
  - appsettings*.json
  - database/*.sql in repo
  **Upload controls**
  - .xlsx/.xlsm whitelist
  - request size limit
  **TLS:** none in MVP (HTTP)
end note

note bottom of BackupZone
  **HA / redundancy (MVP):** NONE — single node, no LB, no Always On.
  **Backup strategy (implemented process):**
  1) SSMS / sqlcmd → full .bak to Backup landing zone
  2) Keep last N bak + git schema.sql as rebuild baseline
  3) Before major demo / import: take fresh bak
  **RPO ≈ 24h** (or last bak before change)
  **RTO ≈ 30–90 min** (install runtime + restore bak + run app)
  **DR drill:** documented restore from bak onto clean SQL instance.
end note

note bottom of Planned
  Future HA options (documented, not claimed live):
  separate DB VM, IIS+TLS, automated backup,
  optional secondary SQL restore-lag standby.
end note

@enduml

' 1. Physical view shows real ports, firewall, ops checks, and an explicit backup landing zone.
' 2. MVP redundancy is honestly NONE; RPO/RTO and restore steps are written on the diagram.
' 3. A grey "planned redundancy" node shows evolution without faking production HA today.
